            <ArticleTitle>Multiple coronary thrombi with cisplatin.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E18-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Testicular cancer is the most common malignancy in young men (15-29 years old). Combination therapy with bleomycin, etoposide, and cisplatin has been the standard first-line treatment for testicular metastatic disease. We present a case of multicoronary thrombi causing acute inferior myocardial infarction in a patient who recently received chemotherapy for testicular tumor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
